<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds ended down but off session lows as European markets recovered with U.S. Treasuries on the back of a NAPM figure broadly in line with market expectations.</p>
<p>&quot;Although European markets are more prudent, the correction in T-bonds has dragged them higher and the negative tone of the session has changed,&quot; said a trader.</p>
<p>The National Association of Purchasing Managers index was 52.6 in August versus 50.2 in July. Markets had forecast a rise to 52.9. Meanwhile, leading indicators rose 0.2 percent in July, down from a 0.5-percent increase in June.</p>
</text>
